# The FastAPI service in api/ ships as a Docker container (see api/Dockerfile),
# never as Vercel Functions. Vercel's zero-config otherwise treats a root-level
# api/ directory as Python serverless functions, which on every build:
#
#   1. installs api/requirements.txt into a Python 3.12 venv, and
#   2. publishes api/app/main.py at /api/app/main
#
# That endpoint 500s on cold start — `from app.models import ...` only resolves
# with the container's WORKDIR on sys.path, not Vercel's /var/task root. It also
# means the public /qr and /batch endpoints are one import fix away from being
# live on the marketing domain with no auth and no rate limiting.
#
# Excluding api/ keeps the Vercel project to what it is meant to be: the static
# Next.js web UI.
api
